\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God, the Rock of Ages,
\par Who evermore hast been,
\par What time the tempest rages,
\par Our dwelling- place serene:
\par Before Thy first creations,
\par O Lord, the same as now,
\par To endless generations
\par The everlasting Thou!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our years are like the shadows
\par On sunny hills that lie,
\par Or grasses in the meadows
\par A sleep, a dream, a story
\par By strangers quickly told,
\par An unremaining glory
\par Of things that soon are old.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Thou, who canst not slumber,
\par Whose light grows never pale,
\par Teach us aright to number
\par Our years before they fail,
\par On us Thy mercy lighten,
\par On us Thy goodness rest,
\par And let Thy Spirit brighten
\par The hearts Thyself hast blessed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, crown our faith's endeavour
\par With beauty and with grace,
\par Till, clothed in light for ever,
\par We see Thee face to face:
\par A joy no language measures,
\par A fountain brimming o'er,
\par An endless flow of pleasures,
\par And ocean without shore.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

